  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "1657-root",
    "title": "AKU faculty awarded Hilal-e-Imtiaz",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "The award is Pakistan's second-highest civilian honour. ",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "d07a52675a6e5bd8",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "1657-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/1657-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "AKU faculty awarded Hilal-e-Imtiaz"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Sheikh Arshad Saeed, the Abdulaziz Hussainali Shariff Professor of Pharmacology, has been awarded the second highest civil award by the government of Pakistan, the Hilal-e-Imtiaz. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Saeed joined AKU in 1984 and has been actively involved in breakthrough discoveries and contributions to knowledge in inflammation, anti-inflammatory drugs, reproductive biology and molecular mechanisms of human platelet aggregation. He holds the rare distinction of discovering nine patented medical procedures, techniques and instruments. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Saeed has an active teaching experience of over two decades and his supervisory role has led to the award of six PhDs and three MPhils from eminent national and international universities. Dr Saeed is also the first Pakistani to be elected as a fellow of the Royal Institute of Biology, London, in 1980. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Saeed acknowledges AKU for providing the infrastructure and motivation for his research work. \"The three of us in pharmacology, Dr Amin Suria, Dr Anwar Gilani and myself have worked together as a team with a positive attitude and a disciplined approach to work. When the University has done so much for us, it also becomes our duty to work with devotion and fervour towards its development and growth.\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
